From 1bd6c85376ddb928880495cec15b281d2c8e4dc9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stephan Raj Ignatious Durairaj <signatio@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Mon, 29 Jun 2026 21:48:30 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Traffic separation design B enablement in prplmesh

This commit brings the necessary plumbing and persistence mechanisms to
fully enable Traffic Separation (TS) in prplMesh, particularly for
OpenWrt/UCI-based systems.

Key changes:

- Derive VAP Type from UCI: Parse `custom_alias` in the `wireless` UCI
  package to determine `vap_type` (HOME, GUEST, VIDEO, etc.) during AP
  HAL initialization (nl80211 / bpl_cfg_wifi). Adds
  `bpl_cfg_get_wifi_credentials_by_ssid()` for SSID-based credential
  lookup when interface-name lookup fails (e.g., MLO link-suffixed ifaces).

- Fallback VAP Type resolution: In `update_vaps_type()`, dynamically
  deduce `vap_type=GUEST` on repeater nodes using the Traffic Separation
  SSID-to-VID mapping when no explicit UCI entry exists (handles
  dynamically-created BSS that arrive before TS policy).

- MLO support for TS: Strip `_linkX` suffixes from VAP interface names
  in `collect_ports_from_db()` to ensure correct access port
  identification and bridge attachment.

- Bridge Mapping Verification (optional): Add `ts_bridge_mapping_enabled`
  flag (UCI: `TrafficSeparation_bridge_mapping_enable`) to optionally
  verify and fix Linux bridge attachments for access and trunk ports at
  runtime via `verify_and_fix_bridge_assignments()`.

- Bridge Assignment Persistence (optional): Add `ts_persistence_enabled`
  flag (UCI: `TrafficSeparation_persistence_enable`) to optionally persist
  guest/private interface bridge assignments into the `network` UCI config
  (modifying the `ports` list of bridge device sections) via
  `persist_bridge_assignments()`. Backhaul BSS always go to the private
  bridge; fronthaul-only BSS are assigned based on `vap_type` with
  fallback to SSID-VID mapping.

- BPL APIs: Introduce new BPL functions for UCI network config
  manipulation:
    - `cfg_get_traffic_separation_bridge_mapping_enabled()`
    - `cfg_get_traffic_separation_persistence_enabled()`
    - `cfg_persist_iface_bridge_assignment()`
    - `cfg_remove_iface_from_bridge_config()`
    - `cfg_commit_network_config()`
    - `cfg_get_bridge_for_iface()`
    - `cfg_get_network_name_for_bridge()`
    - `cfg_set_wifi_iface_network()`
    - `cfg_commit_wireless_config()`
  Implemented for UCI, DM, and Linux platforms.

- Re-read TS feature flags at apply time in `TrafficSeparationTask::reset()`
  to handle the case where UCI is not yet initialized when the agent starts
  (timing issue on first boot).

- Optimized UCI Commit Logic: Avoid unnecessary UCI commits in
  `bpl_cfg_set_wifi_credentials()` if the credentials (ssid, encryption, key)
  have not changed. This prevents netifd from triggering unnecessary hostapd
  restarts on every autoconfiguration cycle.

- Robust Interface Section Matching: Improved `wifi-iface` lookup in UCI by
  falling back to matching the `wifi-device` section if the `ifname` option
  is not explicitly set (which is the default behavior in fresh OpenWrt setups).

- Robust BPL UCI List Manipulation: Added new BPL utilities
  `uci_add_list_option` and `uci_del_list_option` to safely manage bridge
  ports lists without creating duplicate entries.

- Configuration Validation & Cleanup: Added validation for `TrafficSeparation`
  VLAN IDs to strictly enforce the 1-4094 range. Refactored `vap_type` parsing
  in `wbapi_utils.cpp` to reuse `string_to_vap_type`.
  Implemented for UCI, DM, and Linux platforms.

Signed-off-by: Stephan Raj Ignatious Durairaj <signatio@qti.qualcomm.com>
